  "result": "Excellent! All 245 tests pass. The late fee feature is complete.\n\n**Summary of implementation:**\n\n**src/reports.js** \u2014 Added `lateFee(invoice, asOf)` function that:\n- Returns 0 if invoice is not overdue (dueDate >= asOf)\n- Calculates days overdue using `daysBetween(dueDate, asOf)`\n- Gets amount due using `balanceDue()` (respects partial payments)\n- Calculates late fee: `daysOverdue * amountDue * 0.0004` (0.04% per day)\n- Rounds result using `roundCents()` for accurate cent calculations\n- Returns 0 for paid invoices (no amount due)\n\n**test/reports.test.js** \u2014 Added 12 comprehensive late fee tests covering:\n- Not overdue conditions (returns 0 for due date and dates before due)\n- Single day and multiple days overdue\n- Partial payment reflection in fee calculation\n- Zero fee for paid invoices\n- Large invoice amounts\n- Different payment terms (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n- Discounts on invoices\n- Small amounts (rounding edge cases)\n- Integer cent validation\n\n**Complete invoicing system features (245 tests total):**\n1. \u2705 Invoices (creation, lines, totals, discounts, VAT, vouchers)\n2. \u2705 Customers (lookup, tier management, ID normalization)\n3. \u2705 Catalogue (products with pricing and VAT rates)\n4. \u2705 Dates (validation, arithmetic in UTC)\n5. \u2705 Payments (recording, balance tracking, status management)\n6. \u2705 Invoice numbering (year-based counters)\n7. \u2705 Invoice rendering (plain text output)\n8. \u2705 Credit notes (refund tracking with separate numbering)\n9. \u2705 Customer statements (filtered invoices due per customer)\n10. \u2705 Reports:\n    - Overdue invoices (sorted by days overdue)\n    - VAT summary (by rate)\n    - Late fees (0.04% per day)",
